# Architecture Decision Records (ADR)

> **Why this file exists:** stop re-deriving or contradicting settled design. An ADR
> records a decision that is **expensive to reverse** — and only those. Small, easily
> reversed choices do **not** need an ADR.

## When to write one
- Choosing a framework / library / storage that would be costly to swap.
- Defining a cross-cutting contract (response envelope, error model, layering).
- A deliberate constraint or trade-off future-you will otherwise re-litigate.

## How
1. Copy [`TEMPLATE.md`](TEMPLATE.md) → `NNNN-short-title.md` (next number).
2. Fill Context · Decision · Consequences. Keep it short.
3. Status: `Proposed` → `Accepted` (or `Superseded by NNNN`).
4. Link it from the code/doc it governs.

